Z||000000||CanadianGT||08-06-2001||04:36 PM||||If you have been following any of the posts I have made in the last month and a half or so, you will know that I am in the midst of a l awsuit against an engine rebuilder who really messed up my car.  Anyhow, while im waiting for my trial, I am trying to fix all the mistakes he has made that I can ( I have already got a affidafid from another mechanic about all the problems).  Yesterday I fixed the shft linkage, so that when it say's im in Drive I really am.  Now I need help with my Altenator.  The way he put it in, he had it resting against the CV joint, which has cause a complete rip in the boot ( have to fix that later).  Obviously he has the Bracket in the wrong place.  I am wondering how the Bracket goes in.  Does it attatch to the head in any way?  Right now he has just 2 bolts holding it on, but there are 3 holes at the top of the bracket, where it looks as though there are supposed to be 3 bolts.  If anyone has any Idea how this goes on it would be of great help. Thanks in advance.<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||CanadianGT||08-06-2001||09:57 PM||||Anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||08-07-2001||12:32 AM||||Your talking about a 2.8 correct?<BR>If so, yes, the three bolt holes at the top of the bracket mount to the head, the lower ones to the front of the block. Take pictures before repositioning for the judge! Also of damage caused, note down time and repair costs!||||reg||1
